<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lake Peipus</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lake Peipus is a large lake on the border between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it marked the frontier between the lands of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonians">Estonians</a>, conquered by the Livonian crusaders in the 13th century, and the Novgorod Republic. On its frozen surface <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-nevsky">Alexander Nevsky</a> defeated the Livonian Order in 1242 at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-on-the-ice">Battle on the Ice</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lake-peipus.jpg" alt="Lake Peipus" width="320" height="545" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lake_Peipus,_LandSat-8,_2016-10-20.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
